BD-J: implement the HAVi background plane; add bd_bdj_waiting_for_playback()

1. HAVi background plane (behind video).
   HBackgroundDevice.setBackgroundConfiguration() and
   HStillImageBackgroundConfiguration.displayImage() only stored state and
   logged UNIMPLEMENTED, so a disc that paints its menu background through
   them (Lionsgate's com.lge.radius engine, e.g. John Wick 3) showed nothing.
   The plane is now rendered (configuration colour, then the still image
   scaled into its HScreenRectangle) and delivered through the existing ARGB
   overlay callback on BD_OVERLAY_BG, the slot reserved in 1.5.0 (no public
   ABI change). The background never queues BD_EVENT_MENU and never uses an
   application-allocated BD_ARGB_BUFFER. displayImage() decodes into its own
   copy (HBackgroundImage.flush() frees the image's buffers): up to 2 s
   inline, or on a worker when called on an image fetcher thread (discs call
   it from imageLoaded()); a missing image throws IOException. The plane is
   reset on BD-J unload and when the xlet that set it has been terminated.
   updateBackgroundN is registered last so an older jar still registers.

2. bd_bdj_waiting_for_playback(): 1 while a BD-J title has no playlist
   open, 2 while it has prefetched one it has not started, else 0
   (BD_HAVE_BDJ_WAITING_FOR_PLAYBACK). bd_read() delivers nothing
   then (it only idles), so a player blocked in bd_read() can neither present
   the BD-J graphics nor deliver key input - a BD-J screen that plays no
   playlist (e.g. a disc's own resume prompt) is left invisible and dead.

